# cp redis.env.example redis.env and fill it in. redis.env is gitignored.
#
# Redis runs inside the cluster, not on a VM, so there is nothing to fetch — pick one:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 24
#
# It goes into a redis:// URL for the Python services as well as a StackExchange.Redis
# `password=` field for the .NET ones. The URL form is the constraint: @ : / ? # and % have to
# be percent-encoded there. `openssl rand -hex` avoids the question entirely.
REDIS_PASSWORD=
